      "key": "linuxdba1-filesystems-mounts-007",
      "type": "single_choice",
      "text": "What is a mount point in the lab's model?",
      "answers": [
        {
          "key": "a",
          "text": "A directory to which a filesystem is attached",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "key": "b",
          "text": "Always a separate physical disk",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "c",
          "text": "The PID of the mount process",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "d",
          "text": "A PostgreSQL configuration file",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "A mount point is an ordinary directory that becomes the access point to the mounted filesystem.",
      "source": {
